---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /compare/index.html
title: Compare
---

<header class="detail-head">
	<h2 class="page-hed">Comparaison</h2>
	<p class="lede">
		Deux sites s’affichent côte à côte, à partir des séquences d’images que
		Lighthouse a capturées en les mesurant. Le chronomètre indique le temps
		réellement enregistré : une piste plus avancée est donc bien arrivée là
		plus tôt.
	</p>
</header>

{#
L’état sans script et l’état d’erreur affichent le même message : l’animation
est la page. Il est remplacé par la course elle-même une fois le catalogue
chargé. Ainsi, si le script ne se charge pas, le lecteur sait où trouver les
images au lieu de se retrouver avec des commandes inactives.
#}
<div class="panel race-fallback" id="race-fallback">
	<p id="race-fallback-text">
		Cette page anime deux séquences d’images pour les comparer, ce qui nécessite
		JavaScript. La séquence d’images de chaque site se trouve sur sa page,
		accessible depuis <a href="/">le classement</a>.
	</p>
</div>

<div class="race" id="race" hidden>
	<form class="panel race-picker" id="race-picker" autocomplete="off">
		{#
		En premier, car ce choix détermine tout le reste : les pistes, les noms
		proposés et les catégories affichées proviennent tous d’une même capture.
		Deux sites mesurés avec des paramètres de limitation différents
		correspondent à deux connexions différentes ; les placer sur le même axe
		ferait arriver bien plus vite le site non limité, uniquement en raison
		de ses conditions de mesure. Ce contrôle est masqué lorsque le corpus
		ne comporte qu’un seul type de capture : inutile d’afficher un choix
		sans alternative.
		#}
		<div class="race-picker-top">
			<fieldset class="race-throttle" id="race-throttle" hidden>
				<legend>Type de capture</legend>
				{#
				Les mêmes deux symboles que sur les pages des sites, pour que le
				contrôle et l’étiquette de la capture forment un tout. Les symboles
				sont décoratifs : le texte adjacent en donne le sens.
				#}
				<label>
					<input type="radio" name="race-throttle" value="true" checked>
					Limité <span class="tag-mark" aria-hidden="true">🐢</span>
					<span class="race-throttle-count" data-capture="true"></span>
				</label>
				<label>
					<input type="radio" name="race-throttle" value="false">
					Non limité <span class="tag-mark" aria-hidden="true">🐇</span>
					<span class="race-throttle-count" data-capture="false"></span>
				</label>
			</fieldset>
			<div class="race-shuffle">
				<button type="button" id="race-shuffle"><i class="fa-solid fa-play" width="10" height="10" aria-hidden="true"></i> Mélanger</button>
				{#
				Permet de limiter les choix proposés par le bouton de mélange.
				Ce filtre ne fait pas partie de la course elle-même : l’adresse
				conserve les sites, pas la façon dont ils ont été choisis. C’est
				donc un contrôle, alimenté par le catalogue, qui ne propose que les
				catégories comportant des séquences d’images à comparer.
				#}
				<label class="race-category">
					parmi
					<select id="race-category"><option value="">toutes les catégories</option></select>
				</label>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="race-fields" id="race-fields"></div>
		{#
		Une seule liste pour toutes les pistes. La valeur saisie est l’URL
		d’affichage du site ; l’adresse utilise des slugs, comme
		/site/<slug>/.
		#}
		<datalist id="race-catalog"></datalist>
		{#
		Le symbole de suppression est rendu une seule fois ici afin que la
		transformation Font Awesome puisse le convertir en `<use>` pointant vers
			la feuille de sprites de cette page et que le symbole soit inclus dans
			le bundle. Les lignes de piste sont créées dans le navigateur et ne
			peuvent pas utiliser de shortcode à la compilation ; chaque bouton
			Supprimer en clone donc le contenu plutôt que de reproduire le tracé.
			#}
			<span class="race-icon-source" hidden>
			<i class="fa-solid fa-trash-can" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		</span>
			<span class="race-icon-source-lock" hidden>
			<i class="fa-solid fa-lock" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		</span>
			<span class="race-icon-source-unlock" hidden>
			<i class="fa-solid fa-lock-open" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		</span>
			<span class="race-icon-source-finish" hidden>
			<i class="fa-solid fa-flag-checkered" width="10" height="10" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		</span>
			<div class="race-picker-actions">
				<button type="button" id="race-add">Ajouter une piste</button>
				<span class="race-count muted small" id="race-count"></span>
			</div>
	</form>

	<div class="race-controls">
		<button type="button" class="race-play" id="race-play">Démarrer</button>
		<button type="button" id="race-restart">Réinitialiser</button>
		<label class="race-speed">
			Vitesse
			<select id="race-speed">
				<option value="0.25">0,25&times;</option>
				<option value="0.5">0,5&times;</option>
				<option value="1" selected>1&times; temps réel</option>
				<option value="2">2&times;</option>
				<option value="4">4&times;</option>
			</select>
		</label>
		<output class="race-clock" id="race-clock">0 ms</output>
	</div>

	<input type="range" class="race-scrub" id="race-scrub" min="0" max="1000" value="0" step="1"
			aria-label="Parcourir la comparaison">

	<div class="race-scroll" id="race-scroll">
		<div class="race-grid" id="race-grid"></div>
	</div>

	<p class="race-result" id="race-result" role="status"></p>

	<p class="muted small race-note">
		Les images sont des vignettes tirées de la capture Lighthouse médiane sur le
		profil émulé {{ sites.config.formFactor }}. Les temps sont mesurés depuis le
		début de la navigation, puis les images sont rééchantillonnées sur une grille
		commune, puisque chaque exécution les capture selon son propre calendrier.
		Le chronomètre indique le temps enregistré. Chaque séquence ne comporte que
		huit échantillons de sa propre exécution, et Lighthouse adapte la durée de
		cette séquence à celle de l’exécution : une piste s’arrête donc à la fin de
		sa capture, au lieu de conserver sa dernière image sur un axe conçu pour une
		exécution plus longue.
	</p>
	{#
	Deux explications pour la même page, une par type de capture, affichées selon
	le choix effectué en haut du formulaire. Elles ne peuvent pas être réunies
	en un seul paragraphe avec des réserves : la note sur les captures non
	limitées avertit que les images défilent plus vite que pour un visiteur,
	tandis que celle sur les captures limitées explique l’inverse.
	#}
	<div id="race-note-unthrottled" hidden>
		<p class="muted small race-note">
			<strong>Ces images proviennent d’une capture très peu limitée.</strong> Les
			exécutions utilisent la limitation simulée par défaut de Lighthouse, qui ne
			ralentit ni la connexion ni le processeur : la limitation réseau est
			désactivée avant le chargement et aucune limitation du processeur n’est
			appliquée. L’émulation de l’appareil, elle, est bien réelle : la fenêtre
			d’affichage a la taille d’un téléphone et l’agent utilisateur est mobile.
			Il s’agit donc bien de la mise en page {{ sites.config.formFactor }}, mais,
			pour le reste, la page se charge aussi vite que le permettent la machine de
			mesure et sa connexion. Une exception : Lighthouse simule
			<code>requestIdleCallback</code> en ne lui accordant qu’un quart de son
			budget habituel à chaque appel. Une page qui planifie son travail de cette
			façon le répartit donc davantage ici que sur votre machine.
		</p>
		<p class="muted small race-note">
			Le modèle Lantern de Lighthouse applique ensuite un profil 4G lent et un
			ralentissement du processeur par 4 pour estimer le temps de chargement sur
			une connexion lente. C’est de là que viennent les valeurs TTFB, FCP et LCP,
			qui ne sont pas représentées sur cet axe : les images montrent un chargement,
			tandis que ces valeurs décrivent un autre chargement, plus lent, qui n’a
			jamais réellement eu lieu. Les deux sont exacts, mais décrivent des choses
			différentes, et aucun décalage ne peut les faire coïncider : une page peut
			être entièrement affichée dans ces images bien avant le FCP indiqué. La
			ligne d’arrivée correspond donc à ce qui a été observé : le moment où
			l’image d’une piste cesse de changer. Les anneaux à côté de chaque piste
			indiquent les scores du site, qui portent sur le site et non sur ce
			chronomètre. Ceci illustre deux mesures ; ce n’est pas un benchmark.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div id="race-note-throttled">
		<p class="muted small race-note">
			<strong>Ces images proviennent d’un chargement limité.</strong> Les
			exécutions ont appliqué le profil 4G lent de Lighthouse et un ralentissement
			du processeur par 4 directement au navigateur, et non à un modèle après
			coup : la page s’est chargée sur une connexion volontairement lente et un
			processeur volontairement ralenti. Cela se rapproche davantage de ce qu’une
			personne sur téléphone pourrait attendre que ne le ferait une capture sans
			limitation.
		</p>
		<p class="muted small race-note">
			Les marqueurs TTFB, FCP et LCP de chaque piste sont observés dans la même
			trace que ses images ; ils correspondent donc à ce qu’elles montrent. Ils
			proviennent d’un seul chargement limité, et non des exécutions ayant servi
			à calculer le score du site : ils peuvent donc différer des valeurs affichées
			sur sa page. Un résultat serré l’est encore davantage qu’il n’y paraît.
			Les anneaux à côté de chaque piste indiquent les scores du site, qui portent
			sur le site et non sur ce chronomètre. Ceci illustre deux mesures ; ce n’est
			pas un benchmark.
		</p>
	</div>
</div>

<script src="/js/filmstrip-lanes.js"></script>
<script>
/*
 * The race. Everything here is client-side because the pairing is a query
 * parameter and the site is static: one built page has to serve every pairing.
 */
(function () {
	var root = document.getElementById("race");
	var fallback = document.getElementById("race-fallback");
	if (!root || !window.fetch || !window.Map || !window.FilmstripLanes) return;

	var MAX_LANES = 8;

	/*
	 * How far the frames shrink as lanes are added.
	 *
	 * Eight lanes at full size is a race nobody can see the end of without
	 * scrolling past the start of it. The floor matters as much as the curve:
	 * below about half size the label column's own contents set the row height
	 * anyway, so shrinking further costs legibility and buys nothing.
	 */
	function laneScale(count) {
		return Math.max(0.5, Math.min(1, 2.2 / count));
	}

	/*
	 * Durées réelles pour comparer les couloirs.
	 *
	 * L’axe n’est jamais étiré pour les faire tenir ; les repères situés après
	 * la fin de la course ne sont pas dessinés. Les plus longues n’apparaissent
	 * que dans les courses ralenties.
	 */
	var COMPARISONS = [
		{ label: "👁 Clignement d’œil humain", at: 150 },
		/* 60 secondes pour 70 battements. */
		{ label: "💓 Battement de cœur humain", at: 857 },
		/* 384 400 km à 299 792 km/s. */
		{ label: "🌕 Lumière de la Lune à la Terre", at: 1282 },
		/* 40 075 km à l’équateur en un jour sidéral — 465 m/s. */
		{ label: "🌍 La Terre tourne de 1 km à l’équateur", at: 2150 },
		/* Un mile à 343 m/s, la vitesse du son à 20 °C. */
		{ label: "🔊 Le son parcourt un mile", at: 4692 },
		{ label: "🍪 Règle des 5 secondes", at: 5000 },
		{ label: "📹 Vidéo TikTok", at: 6000 },
		{ label: "🏃 Usain Bolt court le 100 m", at: 9580 },
		{ label: "🧼 Lavez-vous les mains (CDC)", at: 20000 },
		{ label: "🏀 Temps d’attaque NBA", at: 24000 },
		{ label: "📺 Publicité télévisée", at: 30000 }
	];


	var grid = document.getElementById("race-grid");
	var scroll = document.getElementById("race-scroll");
	var fields = document.getElementById("race-fields");
	var catalogList = document.getElementById("race-catalog");
	var clock = document.getElementById("race-clock");
	var scrub = document.getElementById("race-scrub");
	var playButton = document.getElementById("race-play");
	var result = document.getElementById("race-result");
	var count = document.getElementById("race-count");

	var catalog = [];
	var bySlug = new Map();
	var byName = new Map();
	var lanes = [];
	/* Categories a random pairing may draw from — see api-race.njk. Empty means
	   no filter. */
	var categories = [];
	/* One of their ids, when Shuffle has been narrowed to a single category. */
	var shuffleCategory = "";
	/*
	 * Which capture the page is comparing: false for unthrottled, true for
	 * throttled. Every lane has to be one or the other — see `matchesCapture`.
	 */
	var captureMode = true;
	var compareMarkers = [];
	var timeline = null;
	var now = 0;
	var playing = false;
	var speed = 1;
	var raf = 0;
	var lastFrameTime = 0;
	var follow = true;

	var L = window.FilmstripLanes;
	var el = L.el;
	var fmtMs = L.fmtMs;
	var settledAt = L.settledAt;

	/*
	 * Les six points des catégories affichés dans les listes « Mesures récentes »,
	 * issus du même `ringBands` que le rapport — les quatre catégories Lighthouse,
	 * puis axe et les Core Web Vitals.
	 *
	 * Des points plutôt que les anneaux du classement : ils s’affichent sur une
	 * seule ligne, à côté du nom d’un site, où six cercles de 24 px prendraient
	 * toute la place au lieu de rester un simple détail.
	 */
	function bandDots(site) {
		var dots = el("span", "recents-dots");
		dots.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "true");
		dots.title = "Performances, Accessibilité, Bonnes pratiques, SEO, Axe, Core Web Vitals";
		(site.bands || []).forEach(function (band) {
			dots.appendChild(el("span", "recents-dot recents-dot-" + band));
		});
		return dots;
	}

	/* The mark from the hidden source in the markup. Empty string if it is
	   missing, which leaves a button with a label and no icon rather than a
	   broken one. */
	function trashIcon() {
		var source = document.querySelector(".race-icon-source");
		return source ? source.innerHTML : "";
	}

	function lockIcon(locked) {
		var source = document.querySelector(locked ? ".race-icon-source-lock" : ".race-icon-source-unlock");
		return source ? source.innerHTML : "";
	}

	/* ------------------------------------------------------------- the lanes */

	function renderGrid() {
		timeline = L.buildTimeline(lanes.map(function (l) { return l.site; }));
		grid.innerHTML = "";
		grid.style.setProperty("--cols", timeline.cols);

		/* Widest frame in the race sets the column, so lanes stay in step even
		   when two sites were captured at different sizes. */
		var aspect = 0.5;
		lanes.forEach(function (lane) {
			var s = lane.site;
			if (s.width && s.height) aspect = Math.max(aspect, s.width / s.height);
		});
		root.style.setProperty("--race-aspect", aspect.toFixed(4));
		root.style.setProperty("--race-lane-scale", laneScale(lanes.length).toFixed(3));

		grid.appendChild(L.renderRuler(timeline));

		lanes.forEach(function (lane, index) {
            // Prepend frame with base path for absolute URL
            lane.site.frames = lane.site.frames.map(frame => ({
                ...frame,src:"{{meta.url}}" + frame.src
            }))
			lane.index = index;
			/* Kept, so the clock can mark the winning row — see setTime. */
			lane.nameEl = renderName(lane);
			lane.laneEl = L.renderLane(lane, timeline);
			grid.appendChild(lane.nameEl);
			grid.appendChild(lane.laneEl);
		});

		renderComparisons();
		lanes.forEach(function (lane) { L.packMarkers(lane, lane.laneEl, timeline, strideWidth()); });
		renderResult(null);
		observeLanes();
	}

	/*
	 * One row of flags, above the lanes they are there to be read against.
	 *
	 * Built after the lanes and inserted in front of them, because packing the
	 * labels needs a rendered frame to measure the column stride from.
	 */
	function renderComparisons() {
		compareMarkers = [];

		var name = el("div", "race-name is-compare");
		var inner = el("span", "race-sticky");
		var title = el("span", "race-name-link");
		title.textContent = "Real world";
		inner.appendChild(title);
		name.appendChild(inner);

		var lane = el("div", "race-lane is-compare");
		var built = [];

		COMPARISONS.forEach(function (item) {
			/* Off the end of this race — see COMPARISONS. */
			if (item.at > timeline.end) return;

			/* Pole and label as siblings under a wrapper that carries neither
			   z-index nor opacity: anything on the wrapper would make a stacking
			   context and trap the label inside it, leaving every label to be
			   crossed by the poles of the flags after it. */
			var marker = el("div", "race-flagpost");
			marker.style.setProperty("--at", item.at / timeline.step);

			marker.appendChild(el("i", "race-flagpost-pole"));

			var label = el("span", "race-flagpost-label");
			label.style.setProperty("--row", 0);
			label.textContent = item.label + " · " + fmtMs(item.at);
			marker.appendChild(label);
			lane.appendChild(marker);

			built.push({ at: item.at, label: label });
			compareMarkers.push({ el: marker, time: item.at });
		});

		var firstLane = grid.querySelector(".race-name");
		grid.insertBefore(name, firstLane);
		grid.insertBefore(lane, firstLane);

		var used = L.packRows(built, timeline, strideWidth());
		lane.style.setProperty("--rows", used);
		name.style.setProperty("--rows", used);
	}

	/*
	 * The label above a lane, on its own line.
	 *
	 * A row of its own rather than a column beside the frames: the frames are the
	 * page, and a name column takes width away from them at every viewport while
	 * a line of text costs one line. The inner run sticks to the left edge so the
	 * name stays readable however far the lane has scrolled.
	 */
	function renderName(lane) {
		var row = el("div", "race-name");
		row.style.setProperty("--lane", lane.index);

		var inner = el("span", "race-sticky");

		var title = el("a", "race-name-link");
		title.href = "/site/" + encodeURIComponent(lane.site.slug) + "/";
		title.textContent = lane.site.name;
		inner.appendChild(title);

		inner.appendChild(bandDots(lane.site));

		lane.flag = el("span", "race-flag");
		lane.flag.textContent = "🏁";
		inner.appendChild(lane.flag);

		row.appendChild(inner);
		return row;
	}

	/* ------------------------------------------------------------- the clock */

	function setTime(t) {
		now = Math.max(0, Math.min(t, timeline.end));
		clock.textContent = L.fmtClock(now);
		if (document.activeElement !== scrub) {
			scrub.value = String(Math.round((now / timeline.end) * 1000));
		}

		compareMarkers.forEach(function (marker) {
			marker.el.classList.toggle("is-on", marker.time <= now);
		});
		var best = null;
		lanes.forEach(function (lane) {
			L.updateLane(lane, now, timeline);

			var settled = settledAt(lane.site);
			if (typeof settled === "number" && settled <= now &&
				(best === null || settled < best)) {
				best = settled;
			}
		});

		/* The flag goes to whoever stopped changing first, as soon as the clock
		   says so rather than at the end.

		   Every lane on the leading time, not the first one found: strips are
		   sampled coarsely and a fifth of all pairings settle on the same frame,
		   where picking one would be inventing a winner out of lane order. */
		lanes.forEach(function (lane) {
			var settled = settledAt(lane.site);
			var won = best !== null && settled === best && lanes.length > 1;
			lane.flag.classList.toggle("is-on", won);
			/* The whole row, not just the flag: a 🏁 in the label column is easy to
			   miss in an eight-lane race. `toggle` with a value is idempotent, so a
			   row that is already the winner does not restart the animation on
			   every frame — only crossing the line, or scrubbing back over it,
			   plays it again. */
			lane.nameEl.classList.toggle("is-winner", won);
			lane.laneEl.classList.toggle("is-winner", won);
		});

		if (follow) L.followPlayhead(scroll, grid, timeline, now);
	}

	function strideWidth() {
		return L.strideWidth(grid, timeline);
	}

	function tick(stamp) {
		if (!playing) return;
		var delta = lastFrameTime ? stamp - lastFrameTime : 0;
		lastFrameTime = stamp;
		setTime(now + delta * speed);
		if (now >= timeline.end) {
			pause();
			renderResult(rank());
			return;
		}
		raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
	}

	function play() {
		if (playing) return;
		if (now >= timeline.end) restart();
		/* Any start is a fresh decision, so a pause the page made on its own no
		   longer applies. */
		autoPaused = false;
		playing = true;
		follow = true;
		lastFrameTime = 0;
		playButton.textContent = "Pause";
		raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
	}

	/*
	 * Stop the clock while nobody can see it, and pick it back up when they can.
	 *
	 * Two ways out of sight: the comparison scrolled off the screen, or the tab in
	 * the background. The second was also a bug — animation frames stop in a
	 * background tab, so the first one back measured the whole absence as a
	 * single frame's worth of elapsed time and the race leapt to its end.
	 *
	 * Only a pause this made is undone by this. A reader who paused it themselves
	 * wants it to stay paused, and coming back to the tab is not a request to
	 * start again.
	 */
	var autoPaused = false;
	var inView = true;
	/* The racer lanes currently on screen — see observeLanes. */
	var visibleLanes = new Set();
	var laneObserver = null;

	function syncVisibility() {
		var showing = inView && document.visibilityState !== "hidden";
		if (!showing && playing) {
			pause();
			autoPaused = true;
		} else if (showing && autoPaused) {
			autoPaused = false;
			if (now < timeline.end) play();
		}
	}

	/*
	 * Watched per lane rather than as one scroll area.
	 *
	 * The scroll area holds the ruler, the reference row and every label as well,
	 * so any of those on screen counted as the comparison being visible — a race
	 * would keep running with nothing but the ruler in view. What matters is
	 * whether any of the frames are, so this counts the racer lanes themselves
	 * and runs while at least one is on screen.
	 */
	function watchVisibility() {
		document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", syncVisibility);
		if (!window.IntersectionObserver) return;
		laneObserver = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
			entries.forEach(function (entry) {
				if (entry.isIntersecting) visibleLanes.add(entry.target);
				else visibleLanes.delete(entry.target);
			});
			inView = visibleLanes.size > 0;
			syncVisibility();
		}, { threshold: 0 });
		observeLanes();
	}

	/* The lanes are rebuilt on every render, so the observer is pointed at the
	   new ones each time rather than left watching elements that are gone. */
	function observeLanes() {
		if (!laneObserver) return;
		laneObserver.disconnect();
		visibleLanes.clear();
		lanes.forEach(function (lane) {
			if (lane.laneEl) laneObserver.observe(lane.laneEl);
		});
	}

	function pause() {
		playing = false;
		cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
		L.commitFollow(scroll);
		playButton.textContent = now >= timeline.end ? "Rejouer" : now > 0 ? "Reprendre" : "Démarrer";
	}

	function restart() {
		cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
		playing = false;
		follow = true;
		L.commitFollow(scroll);
		scroll.scrollLeft = 0;
		setTime(0);
		playButton.textContent = "Démarrer";
		renderResult(null);
	}

	/* ------------------------------------------------------------ the result */

	/* Ranked on the axis the race is actually run on: when each lane's picture
	   stopped changing. */
	function rank() {
		return lanes
			.filter(function (l) { return typeof settledAt(l.site) === "number"; })
			.slice()
			.sort(function (a, b) { return settledAt(a.site) - settledAt(b.site); });
	}

	function renderResult(ranked) {
		/* Emptied rather than hidden: the line holds its own height from the
		   start, so arriving at the end does not shove the note under it down the
		   page just as someone is reading the finish. */
		if (!ranked || ranked.length < 2) {
			result.textContent = "";
			return;
		}
		var winner = ranked[0];
		var next = ranked[1];
		var winnerAt = settledAt(winner.site);
		var margin = settledAt(next.site) - winnerAt;

		if (margin > 0) {
			result.innerHTML = "🏁 <strong>" + escapeHtml(winner.site.name) +
				"</strong> stopped changing first, at " + fmtMs(winnerAt) + " — " +
				fmtMs(margin) + " ahead of " + escapeHtml(next.site.name) + ".";
			return;
		}

		/* Une égalité est l’interprétation la plus juste lorsque les deux sites
		   se stabilisent sur le même échantillon, car les bandes sont trop
		   grossières pour les départager. */
		var tied = ranked.filter(function (l) { return settledAt(l.site) === winnerAt; });
		result.innerHTML = "🏁 Égalité à " + fmtMs(winnerAt) + " — " +
			tied.map(function (l) { return "<strong>" + escapeHtml(l.site.name) + "</strong>"; }).join(" et ") +
			" se sont stabilisés sur la même image.";
	}

	function escapeHtml(value) {
		return String(value).replace(/[&<>"]/g, function (c) {
			return { "&": "&amp;", "<": "&lt;", ">": "&gt;", '"': "&quot;" }[c];
		});
	}

	/* ------------------------------------------------------------ the picker */

	function renderFields() {
		fields.innerHTML = "";

		/* Always at least two rows, however few lanes are filled. A single racer
		   with no second row would look like the page had lost a control rather
		   than like there being nothing to put in it. */
		var slots = Math.max(2, lanes.length);

		for (var slot = 0; slot < slots; slot++) {
			renderField(slot);
		}

		document.getElementById("race-add").disabled = lanes.length >= MAX_LANES;
	}

	function renderField(index) {
		var lane = lanes[index] || null;
		{
			var row = el("div", "race-field");

			var label = el("label", "race-field-label");
			label.htmlFor = "race-site-" + index;
			label.textContent = "Lane " + (index + 1);
			row.appendChild(label);

			var input = el("input", "race-field-input");
			input.id = "race-site-" + index;
			input.type = "text";
			input.setAttribute("list", "race-catalog");
			input.value = lane ? lane.site.name : "";
			if (!lane) input.placeholder = "aucun élément admissible pour le moment";
			input.addEventListener("change", function () {
				var typed = input.value.trim();
				var match = byName.get(typed.toLowerCase()) || bySlug.get(typed);
				/* Refused rather than silently switching the whole field's capture
				   under the other lanes. */
				if (match && !matchesCapture(match)) match = null;
				if (!match) {
					input.setAttribute("aria-invalid", "true");
					return;
				}
				input.removeAttribute("aria-invalid");
				/* The lock belongs to the slot, so choosing a different site for a
				   locked lane keeps it locked. */
				lanes[index] = { site: match, locked: lane ? Boolean(lane.locked) : false };
				commit(true);
			});
			row.appendChild(input);

			/*
			 * Verrouille un couloir pour le conserver lors des mélanges.
			 *
			 * Il s’agit d’un bouton à bascule plutôt que d’une case à cocher :
			 * il modifie l’action d’un bouton sur un couloir précis. Il se trouve
			 * donc sur la ligne de ce couloir et son état indique s’il est activé.
			 * L’activation ou la désactivation redessine la ligne et réévalue
			 * uniquement le bouton « Mélanger » — cela ne modifie pas la
			 * comparaison et n’a donc aucun effet sur l’adresse ni l’animation.
			 */
			if (lane) {
				var lock = el("button", "race-field-lock");
				lock.type = "button";
				lock.innerHTML = lockIcon(lane.locked);
				lock.setAttribute("aria-pressed", lane.locked ? "true" : "false");
				var lockLabel = (lane.locked ? "Déverrouiller" : "Verrouiller") + " le couloir " + (index + 1);
				lock.title = lane.locked
					? lockLabel + " — le mélange le remplacera"
					: lockLabel + " — le conserver lors du mélange";
				lock.setAttribute("aria-label", lockLabel);
				lock.addEventListener("click", function () {
					lane.locked = !lane.locked;
					renderFields();
					updateShuffleState();
				});
				row.appendChild(lock);
				row.classList.toggle("is-locked", Boolean(lane.locked));
			}

			/* Lane 1 is kept until there are lanes to spare; any lane after it can go,
			   down to a field of one — which is a real state now, not a broken one. */
			if (lane && (lanes.length > 2 || index > 0)) {
				var remove = el("button", "race-field-remove");
				remove.type = "button";
				remove.innerHTML = trashIcon();
				remove.title = "Remove lane " + (index + 1);
				remove.setAttribute("aria-label", "Remove lane " + (index + 1));
				remove.addEventListener("click", function () {
					lanes.splice(index, 1);
					commit(true);
				});
				row.appendChild(remove);
			}

			fields.appendChild(row);
		}
	}

	/* ---------------------------------------------------------- the address */

	function slugs() {
		return lanes.map(function (l) { return l.site.slug; });
	}

	function readAddress() {
		var params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
		var raw = params.get("sites") || "";
		return raw.split(",").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);
	}

	function writeAddress(push) {
		var query = "?sites=" + slugs().map(encodeURIComponent).join(",");
		/* Only when it is not the default, so an ordinary link stays short and a
		   shared one carries the speed only because someone chose it. */
		if (speed !== 1) query += "&speed=" + speed;

		var next = location.pathname + query;
		if (push) history.pushState(null, "", next);
		else history.replaceState(null, "", next);
	}

	/*
	 * The speed from the address, if it names one the control offers.
	 *
	 * Checked against the select's own options rather than a list repeated here:
	 * a query can say anything, and an arbitrary multiplier is a way to hand
	 * someone a race that runs at 1000x or backwards.
	 */
	function readSpeed() {
		var raw = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get("speed");
		var value = parseFloat(raw);
		if (!isFinite(value)) return 1;

		var select = document.getElementById("race-speed");
		for (var i = 0; i < select.options.length; i++) {
			if (parseFloat(select.options[i].value) === value) return value;
		}
		return 1;
	}

	/* Address to control and variable, in one place — used on load and on Back. */
	function applySpeed() {
		speed = readSpeed();
		document.getElementById("race-speed").value = String(speed);
		lastFrameTime = 0;
	}

	/* Rebuild everything from `lanes`, and record it. `push` distinguishes a
	   choice someone made — which belongs in history — from the page settling on
	   a default, which does not. */
	function commit(push) {
		renderFields();
		renderGrid();
		restart();
		writeAddress(push);
		updateShuffleState();
	}

	/* ---------------------------------------------------------- the defaults */

	/*
	 * A random pairing, drawn one from the faster half and one from the slower.
	 * Two sites picked at random are usually within a few hundred milliseconds of
	 * each other, which is not a race worth watching; and the alternative — always
	 * opening on the slowest site in the corpus — puts one name in a pillory on a
	 * page anyone can link to.
	 */
	/*
	 * Whether a random pairing may offer this site.
	 *
	 * The categories held back from the home page's Perfect Scores board are held
	 * back here too — the maintainer's own pages, and starter templates whose
	 * demo pages are near-empty by design. A site in several categories counts if
	 * any one of them is drawable. Typing a name and linking to a slug are
	 * unaffected: this narrows what the page offers unprompted, not what it can
	 * show.
	 */
	/*
	 * Same capture as the rest of the field.
	 *
	 * The hard rule on this page. An unthrottled strip is a full-speed load and a
	 * throttled one is a slow connection; put them in adjacent lanes and the
	 * picture says one site is far quicker when all it had was a faster link.
	 * Nothing in the frames reveals which is which, so the comparison has to
	 * refuse the pairing rather than caption it.
	 *
	 * A strip with no recorded method — stored before the field existed — counts
	 * as unthrottled, which is what it was: everything measured so far ran under
	 * Lighthouse's simulated default.
	 */
	function matchesCapture(site) {
		return (site.throttled === true) === captureMode;
	}

	/*
	 * What a draw can actually offer, category aside: the right capture, and a
	 * strip worth animating.
	 *
	 * The category menu counts with this too, so the number beside a category is
	 * the number of lanes it can fill. Counting plain membership instead made the
	 * menu promise more than the pool held — Developer Tooling read 96 against 91
	 * drawable — and Shuffle then disabled itself at a lane count the menu said
	 * was fine.
	 */
	function drawable(site) {
		return matchesCapture(site) && typeof settledAt(site) === "number" && site.distinct > 1;
	}

	function inChosenCategory(site) {
		var groups = site.groups || [];
		if (shuffleCategory) return groups.indexOf(shuffleCategory) >= 0;
		if (!categories.length) return true;
		for (var i = 0; i < groups.length; i++) {
			if (categoryIndex(groups[i]) >= 0) return true;
		}
		return false;
	}

	function inShufflePool(site) {
		return drawable(site) && inChosenCategory(site);
	}

	function categoryIndex(id) {
		for (var i = 0; i < categories.length; i++) {
			if (categories[i].id === id) return i;
		}
		return -1;
	}

	/* Only categories with enough racers to make a race — a name in the list that
	   cannot fill two lanes is a dead end. */
	/* Only sites of the current capture are offered by name, so a typed lane
	   cannot land the field in a mixed comparison. */
	function fillCatalogList() {
		catalogList.innerHTML = "";
		catalog.forEach(function (site) {
			if (!matchesCapture(site)) return;
			var option = el("option");
			option.value = site.name;
			catalogList.appendChild(option);
		});
	}

	/*
	 * Show the capture control only when there is a choice to make.
	 *
	 * Everything measured so far ran unthrottled, so until some of the corpus is
	 * re-measured the other option leads to an empty field. The control appears
	 * on its own the first time both kinds exist.
	 */
	/* Which account of the frames is showing — see the note markup. */
	function setCaptureCopy() {
		var unthrottled = document.getElementById("race-note-unthrottled");
		var throttled = document.getElementById("race-note-throttled");
		if (!unthrottled || !throttled) return;
		unthrottled.hidden = captureMode;
		throttled.hidden = !captureMode;
	}

	function setUpCaptureControl() {
		var fieldset = document.getElementById("race-throttle");
		if (!fieldset) return;

		var throttled = catalog.filter(function (s) { return s.throttled === true; }).length;
		var unthrottled = catalog.length - throttled;

		/* How much is behind each option, so an empty-looking side is explained
		   rather than mysterious mid-rollout. */
		fieldset.querySelectorAll(".race-throttle-count").forEach(function (span) {
			span.textContent = "(" + (span.dataset.capture === "true" ? throttled : unthrottled) + ")";
		});

		/*
		 * Always shown, both options, whatever they hold.
		 *
		 * Hiding the control while one side was empty made the distinction itself
		 * invisible — nothing on the page said these frames were unthrottled, or
		 * that throttled ones were a thing that could exist. An option with nothing
		 * behind it is shown with its zero and disabled rather than removed, so the
		 * choice is visible before it is available.
		 */
		fieldset.hidden = false;

		// Land on a side that has something, whatever a link asked for.
		if ((captureMode ? throttled : unthrottled) === 0) captureMode = throttled > 0;

		fieldset.querySelectorAll("input").forEach(function (input) {
			var count = input.value === "true" ? throttled : unthrottled;
			input.disabled = count === 0;
			input.closest("label").classList.toggle("is-empty", count === 0);
			input.checked = (input.value === "true") === captureMode;
			input.addEventListener("change", function () {
				if (!this.checked) return;
				captureMode = this.value === "true";
				setCaptureCopy();
				fillCatalogList();
				fillCategorySelect();
				shuffle();
			});
		});
	}

	function fillCategorySelect() {
		var select = document.getElementById("race-category");
		if (!select) return;

		/* Rebuilt whenever the capture changes: a category with ten unthrottled
		   sites may have none of the other kind, and offering it would be a menu
		   entry that empties the field. */
		select.innerHTML = "";
		shuffleCategory = "";
		var all = el("option");
		all.value = "";
		all.textContent = "toutes les catégories";
		select.appendChild(all);

		categories.forEach(function (category) {
			var count = 0;
			catalog.forEach(function (site) {
				if (!drawable(site)) return;
				if ((site.groups || []).indexOf(category.id) >= 0) count += 1;
			});
			/* One is enough to list. A single-site field is a real state now — the
			   lane fills and the second row stays empty — and hiding every category
			   until two exist left the menu blank on a capture that has one. */
			if (!count) return;

			var option = el("option");
			option.value = category.id;
			option.textContent = category.name + " (" + count + ")";
			select.appendChild(option);
		});

		/* Picking a category is asking to see that category, so it draws a field
		   straight away rather than arming a button to be pressed next. */
		/* Assigned rather than added: this runs again on every capture change, and
		   addEventListener would stack a handler per rebuild. */
		select.onchange = function () {
			shuffleCategory = this.value;
			shuffle();
		};
	}

	/* However many lanes are open stay open — shuffling is a reroll of the field,
	   not a reset of it. */
	/*
	 * Lanes a shuffle has to leave alone: locked, and still of the capture being
	 * compared. A lock does not outrank the capture rule — a locked unthrottled
	 * lane cannot stay in a throttled field — so one that no longer matches is
	 * released rather than kept.
	 */
	function keptLanes(count) {
		var kept = [];
		for (var i = 0; i < count; i++) {
			var lane = lanes[i];
			kept.push(lane && lane.locked && matchesCapture(lane.site) ? lane : null);
		}
		return kept;
	}

	/* Everything a draw must not pick: the sites already locked in place. */
	function takenBy(kept) {
		var taken = {};
		kept.forEach(function (lane) { if (lane) taken[lane.site.slug] = true; });
		return taken;
	}

	/*
	 * Reroll the unlocked lanes, leaving locked ones exactly where they are.
	 *
	 * However many lanes are open stay open — shuffling is a reroll of the field,
	 * not a reset of it. The draw is from the category's pool less anything
	 * already locked, so a locked site is never also drawn beside itself.
	 *
	 * A pool no bigger than the open slots is not something to shuffle: every
	 * draw returns the same sites, so the button would only reorder lanes and
	 * claim to have found something. Those slots take the pool whole instead —
	 * however few that is — and nothing happens if that is already on screen.
	 */
	function shuffle() {
		var count = Math.max(2, lanes.length);
		var kept = keptLanes(count);
		var open = kept.filter(function (lane) { return !lane; }).length;
		if (!open) return false;

		var taken = takenBy(kept);
		var pool = shufflePool().filter(function (site) { return !taken[site.slug]; });
		var draws = pool.length <= open ? pool.slice() : randomLanes(open, taken);

		var next = [];
		var d = 0;
		for (var i = 0; i < count; i++) {
			if (kept[i]) next.push(kept[i]);
			else if (d < draws.length) next.push({ site: draws[d++], locked: false });
		}

		if (sameSites(next.map(function (lane) { return lane.site; }), lanes)) return false;
		lanes = next;
		commit(true);
		return true;
	}

	/*
	 * Off when pressing it could not produce a different field.
	 *
	 * Two ways that happens. Fewer eligible sites than lanes and a draw cannot
	 * even fill them, so shuffling would shrink the field rather than change it.
	 * Exactly as many and every draw returns the same set, so once those sites
	 * are showing there is nothing left to find — see `shuffle`.
	 */
	function updateShuffleState() {
		var button = document.getElementById("race-shuffle");
		if (!button) return;

		var count = Math.max(2, lanes.length);
		var kept = keptLanes(count);
		var open = kept.filter(function (lane) { return !lane; }).length;
		if (!open) {
			// Every lane is locked: there is nothing for a shuffle to touch.
			button.disabled = true;
			return;
		}

		var taken = takenBy(kept);
		var pool = shufflePool().filter(function (site) { return !taken[site.slug]; });
		var loose = lanes.filter(function (lane) { return !lane.locked; });
		button.disabled = pool.length < open || (pool.length === open && sameSites(pool, loose));
	}

	/*
	 * `count` sites spread across the range, one drawn at random from each band.
	 *
	 * The spread is the point: sites picked uniformly are usually within a few
	 * hundred milliseconds of each other, which is not a race worth watching.
	 * Sorting by settle time and taking one from each of `count` equal bands
	 * generalises the fast-against-slow pairing to however many lanes are open.
	 */
	/*
	 * The site a race opens against: this one.
	 *
	 * Held by slug rather than by name, since the slug is what the address uses
	 * and what survives a display name changing. Null if it has no filmstrip yet,
	 * which drops the page back to a random pairing rather than to an empty lane.
	 */
	var HOME_SLUG = "www-speedlify-dev";

	function homeSite() {
		return bySlug.get(HOME_SLUG) || null;
	}

	/* The opening field: this site against someone, so the page always shows the
	   same question being asked of a different answer. */
	function openingLanes() {
		var home = homeSite();
		if (!home || !matchesCapture(home)) return randomLanes(2);

		var others = randomLanes(2).filter(function (site) { return site !== home; });
		return others.length ? [home, others[0]] : randomLanes(2);
	}

	/* Everything a random draw is allowed to pick from, under the current
	   category. Named because the count matters as well as the contents — see
	   `shuffle`. */
	function shufflePool() {
		return catalog.filter(inShufflePool);
	}

	function sameSites(sites, currentLanes) {
		if (sites.length !== currentLanes.length) return false;
		var here = {};
		currentLanes.forEach(function (lane) { here[lane.site.slug] = true; });
		return sites.every(function (site) { return here[site.slug]; });
	}

	function randomLanes(count, exclude) {
		exclude = exclude || {};
		var free = function (site) { return !exclude[site.slug]; };

		var usable = shufflePool().filter(free);
		/* Widening past the category is fine; widening past the capture is not —
		   that is the one boundary the field cannot straddle, so a thin pool
		   returns short rather than borrowing from the other side. */
		if (usable.length < count) usable = catalog.filter(matchesCapture).filter(free);
		if (usable.length <= count) return usable.slice();

		var sorted = usable.slice().sort(function (a, b) {
			return settledAt(a) - settledAt(b);
		});

		var band = sorted.length / count;
		var picked = [];
		var taken = {};

		for (var i = 0; i < count; i++) {
			var lo = Math.floor(i * band);
			var hi = Math.max(lo + 1, Math.floor((i + 1) * band));
			var pick = null;

			for (var tries = 0; tries < 20 && !pick; tries++) {
				var candidate = sorted[lo + Math.floor(Math.random() * (hi - lo))];
				if (candidate && !taken[candidate.slug]) pick = candidate;
			}
			/* A band can be all duplicates of something already taken when the pool
			   is small; anything unused keeps the lane count intact. */
			if (!pick) {
				for (var j = 0; j < sorted.length && !pick; j++) {
					if (!taken[sorted[j].slug]) pick = sorted[j];
				}
			}
			if (pick) {
				taken[pick.slug] = true;
				picked.push(pick);
			}
		}

		return picked;
	}

	/*
	 * Lanes for a list of sites.
	 *
	 * A link naming exactly one site is a request to compare that site, so its
	 * lane starts locked: Shuffle then finds it opponents rather than replacing
	 * it, which is the only reading of "compare this" that the button can honour.
	 * The site page's filmstrip section links this way.
	 */
	function lanesFor(sites, fromLink) {
		var single = fromLink && sites.length === 1;
		return sites.map(function (site) { return { site: site, locked: single }; });
	}

	function fromAddress() {
		var picked = readAddress()
			.map(function (slug) { return bySlug.get(slug); })
			.filter(Boolean)
			.slice(0, MAX_LANES);
		if (!picked.length) return null;

		/* A link decides its own capture: the first lane sets it and the rest have
		   to match, so a hand-written address cannot open a mixed field. */
		captureMode = picked[0].throttled === true;
		picked = picked.filter(matchesCapture);
		/* One is a valid field — see `shuffle`. Zero is not a link worth honouring. */
		return picked.length ? picked : null;
	}

	/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ boot */

	function start(data) {
		catalog = (data && data.sites) || [];
		categories = (data && data.categories) || [];
		if (catalog.length < 2) {
			fail("Aucune séquence de défilement n’a encore été capturée : il n’y a rien à comparer.");
			return;
		}

		catalog.forEach(function (site) {
			L.trimToSettle(site);
			bySlug.set(site.slug, site);
			byName.set(site.name.toLowerCase(), site);
		});
		fillCatalogList();

		count.textContent = catalog.length + " sites disposent d’une séquence à comparer.";

		var initial = fromAddress();
		// Avant le premier affichage, pour que le côté vide par défaut soit d’abord remplacé.
		setUpCaptureControl();
		lanes = lanesFor(initial || openingLanes(), Boolean(initial));

		setCaptureCopy();
		fillCatalogList();
		fillCategorySelect();
		applySpeed();

		fallback.hidden = true;
		root.hidden = false;

		commit(false);
		bind();
	}

	function fail(message) {
		document.getElementById("race-fallback-text").textContent = message;
	}

	function bind() {
		/* The picker is a form for the sake of the controls in it, not to be
		   submitted: Enter in a lane input would otherwise reload the page onto a
		   query with no `sites` in it at all. */
		document.getElementById("race-picker").addEventListener("submit", function (event) {
			event.preventDefault();
		});

		playButton.addEventListener("click", function () {
			if (playing) pause();
			else play();
		});

		document.getElementById("race-restart").addEventListener("click", restart);

		document.getElementById("race-speed").addEventListener("change", function () {
			speed = parseFloat(this.value) || 1;
			/* Rebased so the change takes effect from here rather than replaying
			   the elapsed time at the new rate. */
			lastFrameTime = 0;
			/* Replaced rather than pushed: changing pace mid-race is not a place to
			   come Back to, and it would otherwise stack an entry per adjustment. */
			writeAddress(false);
		});

		document.getElementById("race-add").addEventListener("click", function () {
			if (lanes.length >= MAX_LANES) return;
			var taken = {};
			slugs().forEach(function (s) { taken[s] = true; });
			var free = catalog.filter(function (s) { return !taken[s.slug] && inShufflePool(s); });
			if (!free.length) return;
			lanes.push({ site: free[Math.floor(Math.random() * free.length)] });
			commit(true);
		});

		// A new field from the button plays straight away, or as soon as the lanes come into view.
		document.getElementById("race-shuffle").addEventListener("click", function () {
			if (!shuffle()) return;
			if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) return;
			if (inView && document.visibilityState !== "hidden") play();
			else autoPaused = true;
		});

		scrub.addEventListener("input", function () {
			pause();
			follow = true;
			setTime((parseInt(this.value, 10) / 1000) * timeline.end);
		});

		/* Scrolling by hand is a decision to look somewhere; the playhead stops
		   dragging the view back until the race is restarted. */
		L.onSidewaysScroll(scroll, function () { follow = false; });

		/* The address is the state, so Back has to mean something here. */
		window.addEventListener("popstate", function () {
			applySpeed();
			var picked = fromAddress();
			if (!picked) return;
			lanes = lanesFor(picked, true);
			renderFields();
			renderGrid();
			restart();
		});

		/* Asking for less motion is not asking for an empty page: the race is laid
		   out finished instead, which is the same information without the
		   animation. The controls still work if it is wanted. */
		watchVisibility();

		var reduced = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)");
		if (reduced && reduced.matches) {
			follow = false;
			setTime(timeline.end);
			renderResult(rank());
			playButton.textContent = "Start";
		} else {
			play();
		}
	}

	fetch("{{meta.url}}/api/race.json")
		.then(function (response) {
			if (!response.ok) throw new Error(response.status);
			return response.json();
		})
		.then(start)
		.catch(function () {
			fail("Impossible de charger la liste des séquences de défilement ; la comparaison ne peut pas démarrer. La séquence de chaque site est disponible sur sa page.");
		});
})();
</script>
